"Termux is a really great terminal emulator. It really puts to use Android's similarities to Linux by allowing you to do just a bit more than normal. Of course, you still can't achieve Root status without actually rooting your phone, nor can you use Termux to root your phone, but anyone who actually knows what rooting is already knows that and why it won't work. There are a few strange issues, like you have to run a shell script with either sh or bash to avoid an access denied error, but those're Android's fault. My only issue is that Termux won't ask for the permissions it needs; you have to manually give Termux these permissions through Android Settings. Just asking at the very start of first run would be perfect. Please, consider this suggestion, Fredrick Fornwall.",4,2018-03-06 22:19:58
